# Lock-Free SPSC Ring Buffer in Rust

## Conceptual Overview

A Single-Producer Single-Consumer (SPSC) ring buffer is a circular buffer where exactly one thread produces items and exactly one thread consumes them. The key insight is that with only one reader and one writer, we can use two atomic variables — `head` (consumer position) and `tail` (producer position) — without locks, relying on careful memory ordering to ensure visibility and ordering guarantees.

